Anna Canteen MIS – Automated ETL and Reporting Pipeline
1. Project Overview
1.1 Objective
The objective of this project is to automate the collection, cleaning, standardization, consolidation, and export of Anna Canteen MIS data from multiple kitchen-level Excel files.
Each kitchen maintains its own MIS files. The Python ETL process collects data from these files and prepares standardized datasets for management reporting and dashboard development.
The processed data can be used to analyze:
•	Daily expenditure
•	Food cost
•	Food cost percentage
•	Income
•	Vegetable cost
•	Gas consumption/cost
•	Diesel consumption/cost
•	Electricity cost
•	Water cost
•	Manpower cost
•	Transportation cost
•	Production and delivery information
•	Food wastage
The final datasets are exported as CSV files and can be consumed by Power BI for reporting and management dashboards.
