7. Processing Log
A processing log is maintained to prevent the program from repeatedly processing unchanged files.
The log contains information such as:
Column	Description
relative_path	Relative location of the processed file
Modified_time	Last modified timestamp of the file
Example:
relative_path                         Modified_time
ATC/COM.xlsx                          2026-09-20 10:30:25
BBL/Maintenance and Utilities.xlsx   2026-09-20 11:15:42
7.1 Skip Logic
Before processing a file, the program checks whether the combination of:
relative_path + Modified_time
already exists in the log.
If the same file and modification time are already present, the file is skipped.
If the file is new or its modification time has changed, the file is processed again.
This provides an incremental-processing approach instead of unnecessarily processing every file during every execution.
