19. Sheet Classification
The workbook contains different worksheets representing different categories of operational data.
The ETL process classifies each worksheet into its corresponding dataset.
The sheet name is first normalized to reduce problems caused by spaces, underscores, or differences in capitalization.
Example:
sheet_key = (
    sheetname.lower()
    .strip()
    .replace("_", "")
    .replace(" ", "")
)
For example:
"Food Wastage"
becomes:
foodwastage
This makes sheet-name matching more reliable.
