29. Large Excel File Considerations
Excel file size does not always represent the amount of actual data.
A worksheet may contain formatting or populated spreadsheet ranges extending to a very large number of rows even when only a small portion contains meaningful data.
When such files are loaded into pandas, memory usage can increase significantly.
Therefore, large source files should be monitored for:
•	Excessive unused rows
•	Excessive unused columns
•	Large formatted ranges
•	Repeated workbook reads
•	Duplicate DataFrames in memory
•	Unnecessary columns
Optimization should be performed after confirming that the ETL process produces correct results.
