35. Key Design Decisions
The following decisions were made during development:
Use Python for ETL
Python was selected because the source data consists of multiple Excel files with inconsistent structures and requires repeated cleaning and transformation.
Use Pandas DataFrames
Pandas provides a convenient structure for cleaning, transforming, validating, and combining tabular data.
Use Kitchen as a Data Attribute
The kitchen name is added during processing so that consolidated datasets retain their source information.
Use Processing Logs
Processing logs prevent unchanged files from being unnecessarily processed again.
Standardize Dates Before Export
Date standardization reduces parsing problems when the output is consumed by Power BI.
Consolidate Similar Sheets
Data from the same type of worksheet across different kitchens is combined into a single dataset for centralized reporting.
